From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: djvalic <djvalic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 14:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] kiln: tell once about Kiln's own boot loader (update ready,
 or installable)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Kiln's own boot loader is installed and updated only by hand, on the
recovery screen's Reboot / Power page, and most people rarely start the
recovery OS. Kiln OS's ad5x-bootloader-notice (a root script, at each
complete start) now writes HELIX_KILN_BL_NOTICE_FILE (S70helixscreen:
/run/ad5x-bootloader-notice) when there is something to do there:
kind=update when Kiln's boot loader is installed and the recovery OS in
slot A carries a newer build, kind=install when the printer still has
Flashforge's boot loader on a board Kiln's supports (after 3 complete
starts). The screen shows it once as a dialog with OK, with the real
menu path (Settings > System > Boot into recovery > Reboot / Power >
Update Kiln's boot loader, or Install Kiln's boot loader
with the guide's address). Only at idle: not while the setup wizard
runs or is required, not while a re-run is requested or 0088's "Run the
setup wizard?" waits, not while a print holds the printer (motion
blocked), not over another dialog; it looks again every 10 s, since the
script writes the file after the screen has started. OK or a backdrop
tap counts as shown, in HELIX_KILN_BL_STATE_DIR
(/data/ad5x/bootloader-notice): update-seen holds the notice's key (the
carried build), so an update notice comes back only for a newer build;
install-dismissed ends the install notice for good. Nothing happens
without the variables, and nothing here writes the boot loader.

The texts are in en.yml and every other language file, as 0088's. Patch
0055's six Settings > System > Boot into recovery strings (the row, its
description, the question and its text, the restart line, the refusal)
were English outside en and ru; they are translated here in de, es, fr,
it, ja, ko, pt, tr and zh, each with its file's own word for recovery
(Wiederherstellung, recuperación, récupération, ripristino, 復旧, 복구,
recuperação, kurtarma, 恢复), so every notice names the row as the screen
shows it. Only the recovery screen's entries (Reboot / Power, Update
Kiln's boot loader, Install Kiln's boot loader) and its
Boot main OS stay English in those languages: the recovery screen shows
them in English there. The Russian names the menus as the Russian
screens show them (Настройки > Система > Загрузить систему
восстановления, then the recovery screen's Питание > Обновить /
Установить загрузчик Kiln). The Chinese and Japanese words are ones the
baked CJK fonts have. Tests in test_kiln_bootloader_notice.cpp (the
file's lines, the gates, once per build, never again after an install
notice, printing, the wizard, another dialog, Russian, German with its
translated row, Boot into recovery and the notice's path in every
language).

Upstream: not applicable (Kiln OS specific)
